proof_tasks (the machine-checked task list) — implementation plan
=================================================================

status: IMPLEMENTED and green (2026-08-12), steps 1-5 and 7; step 6
(bridge) NOT done. spec: D-2026-08-12-machine-checked-task-list.
Sources: mcp/Tools/HOL/MCP_Task_List.thy, with
mcp/Tools/HOL/Tests/MCP_Fixture_Sorry.thy and MCP_Task_List_Tests.thy.

DEVIATIONS, all forced by the fixture (the plan is the record, so they
are written here rather than quietly absorbed):

- A1 came out NEGATIVE, and for a reason this plan did not anticipate.
  The own-proof-body reading does not misclassify — it yields NOTHING.
  Every thm's PBody oracles field is empty, sorry_direct included, so
  the fulfill_norm_proof/promise hazard was beside the point. A1b (walk
  named dependencies) ships instead and classifies correctly.
- the FACT FILTER moved from "do not block on it" to REQUIRED. The
  plan's reasoning — "a sorry'd package theorem is not a thing that
  happens" — is false: a bare `datatype` emits cheated Quickcheck and
  Narrowing generator equations. The kind tag (Markup.kindN =
  Thm.theoremK) is the discriminator, so recap's A2 is settled too.
- A3 inverted: the oracle carries no term at all (and hence no
  position). The tool always read Thm.prop_of, so it is unaffected,
  but the plan's "oracle position as a secondary hint" is retired.
- two traps not in the plan: facts are stored TRIMMED (Thm.transfer
  before touching a proof body, else CONTEXT "No content for theory
  certificate"), and Thy_Info has no entry for a theory DURING the
  build that defines it, so the tests take the theory value from the
  \<^theory> antiquotation.

